            A common pattern is to put one GPU behind a <span class="text-slate-light">Proxmox
            passthrough VM</span>: the host blacklists <span class="text-slate-light">nouveau and the
            nvidia driver</span> and binds the card to <span class="text-slate-light">vfio-pci</span>, then
            hands it whole to a Linux VM running the <span class="text-slate-light">nvidia-open</span>
            driver. Inside that VM, <span class="text-slate-light">Docker + the NVIDIA Container
            Toolkit</span> expose the GPU to as many containers as the work needs — PyTorch, Ollama or
            vLLM, ComfyUI, Jupyter, CI — each requested with a simple
            <span class="text-slate-light">--gpus all</span>, all sharing the one physical card. It isn't
            PVE-only either: the same Docker + toolkit setup runs <span class="text-slate-light">on the
            Arch host bare-metal</span>, sharing the RTX 5090 across containers without a VM in the middle.
