            place</span> — the VM (or the bare-metal host) — while container images carry
            <span class="text-slate-light">no driver at all</span>; the toolkit injects the device and
            matching CUDA libraries at runtime. That keeps images small and portable, lets many isolated
            environments (different CUDA/Python versions, conflicting deps) run side by side on one card,
            and turns GPU workflows into disposable, reproducible containers instead of a hand-tuned host.
          </p>
